to kick off the ASEAN summit the FIFA  president handed out these customized  football shirts to the leaders of the  ten member Association of Southeast  Asian Nations the bloc focuses on  regional unity while embracing each  nations individual culture but much of  the focus recently has been on how  nations outside are impacting ASEAN  Chinese Premier Li Keqiang spoke to the  group's leaders several ASEAN nations  have territorial disputes with China and  he welcomed progress in negotiations for  a code of conduct in the South China Sea  Beijing has been accused of delaying  those talks for years while it built  Islands undisputed reefs in waterways  critical to shipping and thought to have  huge oil reserves underneath Indian  Prime Minister Narendra Modi also met  the leaders he did not mention the  ongoing negotiations between 16  countries on a regional free trade deal  known as our SEP there are reports that  India has raised some concerns but some  think a deal is not far off but won't be  agreed during this summit the fact is  that the region needs this deal the  symbolism of this deal would be enormous  it would become the world's largest  trading bloc half of the world's  population 40% of the global economy and  this region is also going to become the  center of gravity of global trade and  that's something that would be good news  for some ASEAN nations that have been  hurting under pressure from the ongoing  us-china trade war the u.s. downgraded  its representation here at the ASEAN  summit compared to previous years  sending the Commerce Secretary as the  highest-ranking member of the American  delegation some see this as not only as  an indication of the importance the  Trump administration places on this  region but also as an opportunity for  China when all the leaders of the  asia-pacific you know they asked in  related summits when they show up  without the US president counterpart is  going to undermine US interest and also  the interest of the other countries in  the region that are looking for a kind  of a counterbalance to China  so the unity within ASEAN might become  more important than ever as nations  outside the region jostle for influence  Scott Heidler al Jazeera Bangkok
 

